From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] windows.ui.xaml: third-party identity data attributed; faked properties logged once

xbf_ids.txt (and the header generated from it) now names its source -- the XBF ID tables of XbfAnalyzer by Matt Isenhower, https://github.com/misenhower/XbfAnalyzer, commit a45c8eaa8ee662bb94fba65fb4612df5bc4634d6, Apache License 2.0, whose license text is beside it (LICENSE.XbfAnalyzer) -- as third-party factual identity data with no code; the interface and symbol data name windows-rs 0.30.0 as dual-licensed MIT OR Apache-2.0 and taken under MIT. Stub property setters that accept a value and stub getters that give zero now say so once per property in a FIXME, so traces show what a program relies on that is not implemented yet.
---
